#* {{quote-book|en|title=Demystifying Compact Discs: A Guide to Digital Audio|passage=It should be noted that there are industry observers who feel that the whole concept of individually owned music '''software''' could become obsolete, and that in the future no digital consumer medium will exist. Instead, the listener will pay for a cable service whereby he can call up musical selections from a vast central electronic memory—a sort of library of music.|author=Daniel Sweeney|page=161|year=1986|isbn=0-8306-0628-9|publisher=TAB Books|location=Blue Ridge Summit|edition=1st|url=https://archive.org/details/demystifyingcomp00swee}}
